# Cloudflare Pages custom headers (docs/PROJECT_PLAN.md §7.4).
# connect-src names the real apps/api Worker origin — the actual
# *.workers.dev hostname Cloudflare assigned on deploy (account subdomain
# + Worker name, matching the env.production block in
# apps/api/wrangler.toml — name="avash-api-production"), not just the
# Worker name. Keep this equal to VITE_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL (the
# production GitHub Environment variable apps/web is built with) — this
# file has no build-time substitution, so a change to that origin (e.g. a
# custom domain later) must be hand-applied here too. No Gemini domain
# appears here: the browser never calls Gemini directly (§7.4). img-src
# additionally allows the OSM tile host (ADR-013, MAP_TILE_URL_TEMPLATE)
# -- raster tiles are <img> requests, so they belong in img-src, not connect-src.
# connect-src also names the Supabase project origin (HTTPS for auth/REST,
# WSS for the resource-ticker's Realtime subscription, ADR-010) and
# script-src/frame-src name Cloudflare Turnstile's widget script and the
# iframe it renders into (apps/web/src/features/reports/TurnstileWidget.tsx)
# -- like the Worker origin, the Supabase project ref must be hand-kept in
# sync with VITE_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL if the project ever changes.
# worker-src and manifest-src are named explicitly rather than left to
# fall back through child-src/script-src to default-src. Both resolve to
# 'self' either way today, but the fallback chain for worker-src differs
# between browsers and a later tightening of script-src (e.g. adding a
# nonce, which makes 'self' stop applying to workers) would silently
# unregister the service worker and take Web Push down with it — the
# push handler lives in /sw.js, so this is load-bearing, not cosmetic.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://avash-api-production.galibhabibullah786.workers.dev https://kdklmbqkczkaakgswlix.supabase.co wss://kdklmbqkczkaakgswlix.supabase.co; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://tile.openstreetmap.org;
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), notifications=(self)

# The service worker script is the one unhashed, long-lived file whose
# staleness is self-perpetuating: browsers revalidate it on their own
# schedule, and a cached copy keeps serving the OLD push handler to
# everyone already subscribed. Vite fingerprints every other asset, so
# this exemption applies to exactly one file.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
